gnome-shell on 64-bit SPARC illumos: link gnome-shell (and the run-js-test
helper) with the ADDR32 software capability.

libmozjs-140 is tagged ADDR32 on sparcv9 (library/mozjs-140 in this repo,
patches/10-sparc-addr32.patch), because SpiderMonkey's Values need pointers
below 2^47 and 64-bit SPARC maps near the top of the address space
(https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=577056).  The runtime linker
refuses an ADDR32 library in a process that is not ADDR32 itself.
Oracle Solaris does the same with a RESERVE_SEGMENT mapfile
(oracle/solaris-userland components/gnome/gnome-shell/patches/08_VM.sparc);
illumos ld has no RESERVE_SEGMENT.  Only active for host sunos/sparc64.
Applied on SPARC only (Makefile, ADDITIONAL_PATCHES).  Not submitted upstream.

--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -308,6 +308,13 @@
 po_dir = join_paths(meson.current_source_dir(), 'po')
 
 subdir('js')
+# 64-bit SPARC on illumos/Solaris: libmozjs (through gjs) is tagged ADDR32,
+# so programs linking it must be too (src/sparc-addr32.mapfile).
+addr32_link_args = []
+if host_machine.system() == 'sunos' and host_machine.cpu_family() == 'sparc64'
+  addr32_link_args = ['-Wl,-M,' + (meson.project_source_root() / 'src' / 'sparc-addr32.mapfile')]
+endif
+
 subdir('src')
 subdir('po')
 subdir('data')
--- a/src/meson.build
+++ b/src/meson.build
@@ -254,6 +254,7 @@
   ],
   dependencies: gnome_shell_deps + [libshell_dep, libst_dep, mutter_dep],
   include_directories: [conf_inc, st_inc, include_directories('tray')],
+  link_args: addr32_link_args,
   build_rpath: mutter_typelibdir,
   install_rpath: install_rpath,
   install: true
@@ -280,6 +281,7 @@
 executable('run-js-test', 'run-js-test.c',
   dependencies: [mutter_dep, mtk_dep, gdk_pixbuf_dep, gio_dep, girepository_dep, gjs_dep],
   include_directories: [conf_inc],
+  link_args: addr32_link_args,
   link_with: libshell,
   build_rpath: mutter_typelibdir,
 )
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/sparc-addr32.mapfile
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+# illumos/Solaris 64-bit SPARC: SpiderMonkey's Values hold pointers of at
+# most 47 bits, and libmozjs is tagged ADDR32, so every program that loads
+# it must run in a 32-bit address space (the runtime linker refuses
+# libmozjs otherwise).
+$mapfile_version 2
+CAPABILITY {
+	SF += ADDR32;
+};
